IN PLAIN WORDS
The pattern for every Elusion RPG page: a dark body, the shared .main-nav, and a centered .page-wrapper. Card rows use flex with center, wrap and gap; cards get padding, a border, rounded corners and a max-width. The home page has a hero section with a centered title and a button.

CODE
```css
body { background-color: #111; color: #f5f5f5; }

.page-wrapper {
  max-width: 960px;
  margin: 0 auto;                 /* centers the block */
  padding: 0 20px 40px;
}

.stats-grid, .follow-grid, .contribute-options {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;                /* cards wrap on small screens */
  gap: 20px;
}

.stat-card, .follow-card, .contribute-card {
  padding: 16px 24px;
  border: 1px solid #4fd1ff;
  border-radius: 8px;
  max-width: 280px;
}

.hero { text-align: center; padding: 60px 20px; }
.hero-btn {
  display: inline-block;
  margin-top: 20px;
  padding: 10px 18px;
  background: #4fd1ff;
  color: #111;
  text-decoration: none;
  border-radius: 4px;
}

.stats {
  background-image: url("images/community-bg.png");
  background-size: cover;
  background-position: center;
}
```

KEY POINTS
- gap gives clean spacing between flex items, better than margins everywhere.
- max-width stops cards stretching too wide.
- Keep the important part of a background image in the center 960px.

CORRECTION
The notes had border-radius: 6px–8px; and max-width: ~260–280px;. CSS needs a single value, and the browser ignores lines like those, so the code uses 8px and 280px.

IN PLAIN WORDS
Wrap code in DOMContentLoaded so the HTML exists first. addEventListener("click", healPlayer) runs a function on every click (pass the name without parentheses). A variable like health keeps its value between clicks. classList.add / remove / contains switches modes.

CODE
```javascript
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
  const healBtn = document.getElementById("healBtn");
  const healthText = document.getElementById("healthText");
  let health = 50;

  function healPlayer() {
    if (health >= 100) {
      alert("You are already at full health!");
      return;
    }
    health = Math.min(health + 10, 100);
    healthText.textContent = `Health: ${health}`;
  }

  healBtn.addEventListener("click", healPlayer);   // no () here

  document.body.classList.add("fire-off");
  document.body.addEventListener("click", () => {
    const on = document.body.classList.contains("fire-on");
    document.body.classList.toggle("fire-on", !on);
    document.body.classList.toggle("fire-off", on);
  });
});
```

```css
.fire-off { cursor: url("images/unlitfirecursor.png") 16 16, auto; }
.fire-on  { cursor: url("images/firecursor.png") 16 16, auto; }
```

KEY POINTS
- Template strings (`Health: ${health}`) mix text and variables.
- Clicks go 60, 70, 80, 90, 100; the next one shows the "full health" alert.
- 16 16 is the cursor's hotspot inside a 32×32 image.
- Most browsers show only the first frame of a GIF cursor, and cursor images have a size limit; 32×32 PNGs are safest.

