  align-items: flex-start;
  padding: 1.5rem;
  border: 2px solid #444;
  border-radius: 12px;
}
.kingdom-controls { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
```

KEY POINTS
- type="button" keeps a button from submitting a form.
- Five copies of the same 6 lines → one function called five times.

IN PLAIN WORDS
Load real data from the REST Countries API. On click: check the input, fetch with an encoded name, check response.ok, parse the JSON, guard against empty data, then put the name, capital and region on the card. try/catch shows a friendly message instead of crashing.

CODE
```javascript
kingdomButton.addEventListener("click", async () => {
  const newName = kingdomInput.value.trim();
  if (!newName) return;
  try {
    const response = await fetch(
      `https://restcountries.com/v3.1/name/${encodeURIComponent(newName)}`
    );
    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);
    const data = await response.json();
    if (!Array.isArray(data) || data.length === 0) throw new Error("No match");

    const country = data[0];
    kingdomName.textContent = country.name.common;
    capitalValue.textContent = country.capital?.[0] ?? "No capital listed";
    regionValue.textContent = country.region;
  } catch (error) {
    console.log("Error fetching country:", error);
    kingdomName.textContent = "Country not found";
    capitalValue.textContent = "";
    regionValue.textContent = "";
  }
});
```

KEY POINTS
- await fetch → the response. await response.json() → the data.
- The API returns an array: data[0].name.common, data[0].capital[0], data[0].region.
- ?. stops safely when a field is missing; ?? supplies a fallback.

CORRECTION
- An entry with no capital made capital[0] throw, so the catch said "Country not found" for a country that was found. The code uses capital?.[0] with a fallback.
- An empty input called the API anyway; now it returns first.
- The name is wrapped in encodeURIComponent so spaces and symbols are safe.
